  "facts": [
    "The Talmadge Memorial Bridge, completed in 1991, stretches 1.9 miles across the Savannah River, featuring a 1,100‑foot cable‑stayed main span that replaced the 1953 cantilever truss bridge.",
    "With 185 feet of vertical clearance, the bridge now lets oceangoing vessels pass, a critical upgrade for Savannah’s status as the nation’s fourth‑busiest seaport.",
    "In 2023, GDOT announced the bridge will be raised and eventually replaced, a project projected to cost over $1 billion to accommodate future Neo‑Panamax ships."
